# The thread module's pre-1.0 apidiff allowances: one exact apidiff
# line per acknowledged incompatibility, under the justification that
# reviewed it. Anything not listed fails the build (scripts/apidiff.sh
# "" thread, `make apidiff-thread`). The gate diffs against the newest
# thread/v* tag, so the entries of a cycle are dropped when its tag is
# cut; an entry apidiff no longer reports is dead and is removed with
# the change that made it so.
#
# The API is not frozen: the freeze — the first pair of tags gated
# with this file empty — is deferred until the API is stable. Until
# then a deliberate break is listed here, never smuggled past the gate.
#
# 2026-10-01 review fix train (WEFT-THREAD-REVIEW-2026-10-01.md) —
# pre-1.0, not frozen. Every line below is a deliberate break made by
# the train against thread/v0.8.1, reviewed in its lanes:
#
#   approvals   WithApprover takes its timeout (ApproverTimeout is
#               gone: an Approver without a bound was either never
#               consulted or blocked the turn); ApprovalAuditEntry
#               lists the decisions a resume applies (a slice field).
#   compaction  the hook verdicts Proceed and Cancel are functions,
#               not mutable package variables; token counts are int64
#               throughout (Estimator.Estimate, SummaryMaxTokens,
#               SummaryInput.MaxTokens); Trimmer.Trim returns an error
#               and the trim is recorded in the entry (TrimReport is
#               gone); Instructions is SummaryInstructions and
#               Disabled is NoAutoCompact (the old names collided with
#               the core's and said nothing); the dead fields
#               Compaction.FilesModified, Preparation.SplitPrefix,
#               Summary.Reason and SummaryInput.SummaryModel are
#               removed.
#   core        ErrNotImplemented is removed (nothing returned it);
#               CorruptError unwraps to ErrCorrupt and its cause.
#   backends    OpenConfig and ResolveOpen moved to thread/backend
#               (Config, Resolve): backend plumbing, off the user
#               package; Memory accepts the open options.
#   pool        Wrap and Register return errors; Cancel and Forward
#               take a context and the parent session (a receipt is
#               its session's); Decide records and arms and no longer
#               waits, so it returns no Turn; Receipt.State is the
#               typed State.
(*CorruptError).Unwrap: changed from func() error to func() []error
./pool.(*Pool).Cancel: changed from func(string) error to func(context.Context, *github.com/weftgo/weft/thread.Session, string) error
./pool.(*Pool).Decide: changed from func(context.Context, *github.com/weftgo/weft/thread.Session, ...github.com/weftgo/weft/thread.Decision) (*github.com/weftgo/weft/thread.Turn, error) to func(context.Context, *github.com/weftgo/weft/thread.Session, ...github.com/weftgo/weft/thread.Decision) error
./pool.(*Pool).Forward: changed from func(context.Context, string, github.com/weftgo/weft.Message) (*github.com/weftgo/weft/thread.Turn, error) to func(context.Context, *github.com/weftgo/weft/thread.Session, string, github.com/weftgo/weft.Message) (*github.com/weftgo/weft/thread.Turn, error)
./pool.(*Pool).Register: changed from func(string, *github.com/weftgo/weft.Agent) to func(string, *github.com/weftgo/weft.Agent) error
./pool.(*Pool).Wrap: changed from func(string, string, *github.com/weftgo/weft.Agent, ...WrapOption) *github.com/weftgo/weft.ToolDef to func(string, string, *github.com/weftgo/weft.Agent, ...WrapOption) (*github.com/weftgo/weft.ToolDef, error)
./pool.Receipt.State: changed from string to State
ApprovalAuditEntry: old is comparable, new is not
ApproverTimeout: removed
Cancel: changed from var to func
Compaction.FilesModified: removed
Disabled: removed
ErrNotImplemented: removed
Estimator.Estimate: changed from func([]github.com/weftgo/weft.Message) int to func([]github.com/weftgo/weft.Message) int64
Instructions: removed
Memory: changed from func() Storage to func(...OpenOption) Storage
OpenConfig: removed
Preparation.SplitPrefix: removed
Proceed: changed from var to func
ResolveOpen: removed
Summary.Reason: removed
SummaryInput.MaxTokens: changed from int to int64
SummaryInput.SummaryModel: removed
SummaryMaxTokens: changed from func(int) SessionOption to func(int64) SessionOption
TrimReport: removed
Trimmer.Trim: changed from func(context.Context, []github.com/weftgo/weft.Message) ([]github.com/weftgo/weft.Message, TrimReport) to func(context.Context, []github.com/weftgo/weft.Message) ([]github.com/weftgo/weft.Message, error)
WithApprover: changed from func(Approver) SessionOption to func(Approver, time.Duration) SessionOption
